WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.530
Small-budget ads that bring orders, not just likes.

2
00:00:03.880 --> 00:00:08.530
This is the video for module three of Social Media Marketing for Business.

3
00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:17.970
Paid social means paying a platform to show your content to more people. Boosting is quick. Meta Ads Manager gives more control.

4
00:00:19.220 --> 00:00:23.340
Good targeting puts your money in front of people who can actually buy.

5
00:00:24.590 --> 00:00:29.150
Your picture or video, and your words, decide whether people stop and act.

6
00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:37.000
And the real question is never just how much to spend. It is how much you can afford to pay for one customer.

7
00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:46.540
Grace sells frozen chicken in Abuja. Her Reel of her clean cold room already had more comments than usual, so she chose it.

8
00:00:47.790 --> 00:00:52.770
She taps Boost and chooses Get more messages, with WhatsApp as the destination.

9
00:00:54.020 --> 00:01:01.610
Her audience is people aged 25 to 55 within about 15 km of her shop, the area she delivers to.

10
00:01:02.860 --> 00:01:12.100
Her budget is about 2,000 naira a day for 5 days, about 10,000 naira in total. Start with an amount you can afford to lose while learning.

11
00:01:13.350 --> 00:01:24.080
She saves a price list quick reply, because ads that bring messages nobody answers waste money. After 5 days she records spend, conversations and orders.

12
00:01:25.330 --> 00:01:39.070
Joy sells wigs in Port Harcourt. Her cold ad set showed a Reel of a wig being installed to women in Rivers State interested in hair care. It brought 28 chats at about 375 naira each.

13
00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:53.590
Her warm ad set retargeted people who engaged with her Instagram in the last 60 days, with prices and a WhatsApp button. It brought 42 chats at about 250 naira each, and more orders.

14
00:01:53.940 --> 00:01:57.970
Do not target all of Nigeria if you only deliver in one city.

15
00:01:59.220 --> 00:02:06.940
Uche runs a laundry service in Enugu. Ad A was a designed flyer with the words, quality laundry services, call now.

16
00:02:08.190 --> 00:02:22.590
Ad B was a 12-second video of a rider collecting a bag and the clothes returned folded. Its first line named the problem: too busy for laundry this week? We pick up, wash, iron and return in 48 hours.

17
00:02:23.840 --> 00:02:31.860
He ran both to the same audience at about 1,000 naira a day each, for 7 days, changing only the creative and words.

18
00:02:33.110 --> 00:02:42.580
Ad A brought 9 chats. Ad B brought 31. Real products in use, a short benefit, and one clear button usually beat a crowded flyer.

19
00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:50.280
Here is the most important calculation in this module. Rukayat sells pepper soup packs in Lagos.

20
00:02:51.530 --> 00:03:05.910
Each pack sells for about 6,500 naira. After ingredients, packaging and delivery she keeps about 2,500 naira. That is her break-even cost per order. Ads must cost less than this.

21
00:03:07.160 --> 00:03:22.810
She spends about 2,000 naira a day for 7 days, 14,000 naira in total. The ad brings 40 conversations, so 350 naira each. From those chats she gets 10 orders, a conversion rate of 25 percent.

22
00:03:24.060 --> 00:03:39.960
Cost per order is 14,000 divided by 10, which is 1,400 naira. That is below 2,500, so each order still leaves about 1,100 naira profit after ads. The ad pays.

23
00:03:41.210 --> 00:03:46.950
Every week on the same day, record spend, conversations and orders from your WhatsApp labels.

24
00:03:48.200 --> 00:03:55.810
New ads go through a learning phase, and small budgets can stay there. So avoid editing every day, and judge over a week.

25
00:03:57.060 --> 00:04:01.820
If cost per order climbs above your break-even, pause and freshen the creative.

26
00:04:03.070 --> 00:04:10.640
If it stays below break-even, raise the budget gradually, by about 20 percent at a time, never doubling overnight.

27
00:04:11.890 --> 00:04:22.940
Add your payment method only inside Meta billing, and set an account spending limit while you learn. Never send money or your login to someone offering to run your ads cheaply.

28
00:04:23.290 --> 00:04:31.100
And follow the ad rules. Never claim a product cures a disease, and never use fake discounts or someone else's photos.

29
00:04:32.350 --> 00:04:48.460
To remember. Boost posts that already work. Target where you deliver, and retarget warm people. Show the real product in use with one clear button. Keep cost per order below profit per order. And set a spending limit and make only honest claims.

30
00:04:49.710 --> 00:04:58.860
Now write your one-page ad plan, build two audiences, create two ad versions, and work out your break-even cost per order before you spend.

31
00:04:59.210 --> 00:05:01.360
Then continue with the lessons below.
